<h1> Virtual Network (Azure)</h1>
In this lab, youll work through a set of tasks that will show you how to set up a virtual network.
setting up the recource group, virtual network and virtual machine. Completing this lab, you will gain hands-on experience in creating 
and managing virtual networks in Azure

<h2>Environments and Technologies Used</h2>

- Microsoft Azure (Virtual Machines/Computer)

<h2>Operating Systems Used </h2>

- Windows 10 (21H2)

<h2> Creating Virtual Machine Tasks </h2>

- Task 1: Create a resource group
- Task 2: Create Virtual Machine

<h2> Task 1 </h2>


-  In the Azure portal, search for Resource Group and Click Create
<img width="1351" height="308" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6cc1c2d4-6f06-4583-96df-01ab04b08b8d" />

- Supscription: select Azure subscription 1
- Resource group: Select Lab-test or your preferred Resource Group Name that would be that lab.
- region select Canada Central
- Then click Review + Create
</p><img width="757" height="907" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/faf831e3-eed9-48c6-a946-cb3b778397a8" />


<h2> Task 2 </h2>
- Navigate to the Azure portal and search for `Virtual machines.` - Click `+ Create` and select `+ Azure virtual machine` from the dropdown list.
<img width="718" height="820" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8480dd08-878d-485e-813a-c6c89f26ff18" />
<img width="757" height="656" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01e0601c-f335-4a54-8336-83661a3badb3" />
</p>

- On the Basics tab of the Create virtual network blade, provide the following details:
- Subscription: Select the Azure subscription for this lab.
- Resource group: Click on Create new and enter the name Lab-test.
- Name: Enter myVirtualM.
- Region: Select Canada or a region that would be nearest to you
<img width="1426" height="854" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e5f4a831-9d66-4bfa-8d09-eab08db9c1f0" />

- Scroll Down
- Image: Choose Windows Server 2022 Datacenter: Azure Edition - x64 Gen2
- Size: Select Standard D2s v3
- Username: Azureuser
- Password: Use your personal password.
- Confirm password: Retype your password.
- Public inbound ports: Set it to 'None'
- Would you like to use an existing Windows Server License: 'Leave selection unchecked`

</p>
<img width="940" height="815" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9c4b043a-0499-4c96-b872-ec6cde7f23b6" />

- "Next: Disks" and then Click "Next: Networking"
-  Create new Virtual Network
-  name it Lab2-Vnet
-  Under "NIC network security group," choose None
-  After that just click review + Create
   <img width="763" height="842" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e206f45-1dc4-4c99-81c1-76212ef82584" />

- Congradulation on creating a Virual Machine

